{
  "version": "stethofuse-clinical-targets-v3",
  "declared_utc": "2026-11-20",
  "declaration": "v3 keeps every v2 setting (audio, split seed, test fraction, models, pass bars, gate) and changes only the COPD and pneumonia targets, which v2 could not test because ICBHI has no healthy adults. Declared before any v3 result. (1) Each lung target pools labelled sources: ICBHI, KAUH (Fraiwan et al. 2021, CC BY 4.0) and, for COPD, RespiratoryDatabase@TR (Altan et al., CC BY 4.0). (2) A source is used only if it has both classes inside the supported ages (require_both_classes_per_dataset), so no site contributes only one class. (3) Because sites differ in class mix, the baseline for these targets is site_prior: a model that knows only which dataset a recording came from. A model must beat it (paired AUROC difference, lower 95% bound above 0), so learning the hospital or device earns nothing. (4) The test split is stratified by site and class together, and results are reported per dataset. (5) RespiratoryDatabase@TR releases no per-patient ages; its published cohort range (38-68 years) lies inside the supported adult groups. Its COPD0 group means normal spirometry with chronic symptoms (GOLD 'at risk'): a no-COPD control, not a healthy volunteer. (6) KAUH exports each recording with three Littmann filters; only the extended-range export (E, 20-1000 Hz) is used so a patient counts once. (7) The Fortis (New Delhi) lung set was downloaded and excluded: no patient identifiers or ages, duplicated files, and heart sounds inside its normal class, so a patient-held-out split is impossible.",
